MENTOR: So Sign turns from the middle of its letters, its center.

Sign's pivot starts on its baseline, under the letters, not in their middle. Right now it sits somewhere along that line rather than at one of the clean spots, so if you turned Sign now it would swing around a point below the words.

Two terms to keep apart. **Anchor Point** is where the pivot sits inside the layer. **Position** is where that pivot sits in the comp. If you change Anchor Point alone, the layer slides so the new pivot lands where the old one was. Pan Behind changes both together, so nothing moves on screen.

The frame I pulled at 0 s didn't show me much, but Sign sits in the lower-left part of the comp. That's the layer you're working on.

**How to set it:**
1. Press **Y** for the Pan Behind (Anchor Point) tool.
2. Select Sign in the timeline so its crosshair shows.
3. Start your drag right on the crosshair and drag it up into the middle of the letters.
4. With Sign selected, press **A**, then **Shift+P**. Anchor Point and Position both show, so you can watch them change together while Sign stays put.

Give it a go and tell me "done" when you've set it. I could show you on Door first, if you like.

