Right now Lid's pivot sits outside the lid, below it, which is why it would swing wide. Click Lid in the timeline and its crosshair shows up below the shape; start your drag there.

Two words this lesson uses: **Anchor Point is where the pivot sits inside the layer; Position is where that pivot sits in the comp.** If you change Anchor Point alone, the layer slides so the new pivot lands where the old one was. Pan Behind changes both together, so nothing moves on screen.

Lid is a wide, short shape in the upper-left part of the frame at 0 s. Once its pivot is in its middle, it'll turn in place like a coin spinning on a table, instead of swinging around a point beneath it.

